+    // Find the control to draw by its HWND rather than by id: ids are not
+    // guaranteed to be unique (FileZilla and other apps create many controls
+    // with the same id), in which case FindItem(id) could return the wrong
+    // control -- or a non-owner-drawn one such as a static text -- leaving the
+    // actual owner-drawn control (e.g. a checkbox in dark mode) unpainted. The
+    // HWND from the DRAWITEMSTRUCT always identifies the right control. Fall
+    // back to the id-based lookup just in case.
+    HWND hwndItem = ((DRAWITEMSTRUCT *)itemStruct)->hwndItem;
